@tradition slow-stretch
// W3 rec deck words. Sundays 08:30-09:15 from Day 7, the float room; Dr. Nandakumar leads a stretch at a fifth of a g, 3 to 6 people. Tap to join.
== mail
- Slow stretch tomorrow, {time} in the float room. Dr. Nandakumar leads a gentle stretch at a fifth of a g. Bring water. She'll ask.
== ask
- Slow stretch this morning. It's like stretching in honey. In a good way.
- Coming to slow stretch? Nandakumar says it's good for us. That settles it.
== here
- Slowly. Slower than that.
- Breathe out. Now drink some water.   #funny
- Reach. And float. And reach.
== thanks
- You join the small circle in the float room. Dr. Nandakumar counts, slowly, and your whole back says thank you.   #warm
== chatter
- My back's never been happier than after slow stretch.
- Nandakumar made everyone drink water halfway through slow stretch. In low gravity. It went everywhere.   #funny
